        <p>be supplied from six single-ended boiler: and seventeen others of the Yarrow type, rhe armour-plating is .to be six inches thicli At, the belt, casemates, and .barbettes, four- and a-half inches on the bulkheads, and ten ~nches at the conning tower. The Hampshire 'S a sister ship to the Devonshire, Argyll, 'Roxburgh, Antrim, and Carnarvon.</p>
