      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-10-03_WidnesExaminer_art0035" n="art0035">
        <head>DUKE OF RICHMOND.</head>
        <p>THE DUKE OF RICHMOND.</p>
        <p>Charles Henry Gordon-Lennox, K.G., sixtn Duke of Richmond, first Duke of Gordon, who died on Sunday morning, was the eldest son of Charles, fifth Duke of Richmond, by his marriage with Lady Caroline Paget, daughter I of Henry William, first Marquess of Anglesey. He was born at Richmond House. White-</p>
        <p>hall, on Febru-</p>
        <p>ary- 27th, 18.18:</p>
        <p>educated</p>
        <p>at Westminster</p>
        <p>and at Christ Church, Oxford,</p>
        <p>. graduating B.A. in 1839. In May of that year he entered ' the army, and</p>
        <p>after serving in</p>
        <p>the Royal Horse</p>
        <p>GuSrds' till Sep-</p>
        <p>tember, 1844,</p>
        <p>was then placed on half-pay, but did not finally</p>
        <p>retire from the</p>
        <p>army till July, THE LATE DUKE OF RICH- -1881, when he MOND AND GORDON, K.G. received the</p>
        <p>• honorary rank of major. To the opinion : which he professed upon his election to the House of Commons in 1841 he adhered throughout his life. ,He was a convinced and ' strong supporter of the agricultural industry, voted for the protection of agriculture in 1846, and a year later held the office of President of the Board of Trade. This he held through the remainder of Lord Derby's period of office, and throughout Mr. Disraeli's first Ministry from February till December, 1868. After the death of Lord'Derby the Duke became leader of the Conservative party in the Upper House, and when that party returned to power in February, 1874, he was appointed Lord President of the Council, being two years later created Earl of Kinrara and Duke of Gordon in the peerage of the United King- dom. After the passing of the Act creating a ,Secretarvi of State for Scotland, the Duke was appointed first holder of the office, being also ex-officio Keeper of the Great Seal of Scotland, and Vice-President of the Committee of Coun- cil on Education in Scotland. This office was the last political appointment of his official life.</p>
