      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-10-03_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>FRIGHTENED GIRL'S TALE. Strange Sequel After Ten Years.</head>
        <p>A FRIGHTENED GIRL'S TALE. Strange Sequel After Ten Years.</p>
        <p>A Liverpool girl who experienced a nervous shock ten years ago, has been the victim of a strange series of misfortunes ; the story of her life since then is a lesson to all afflicted with "nerves." In the course of an interview with a representative of the press, Annie i ' Guy, the girl n question, -elated the facts: "Tea rears 'a:go I sustained a very severe shock to the Lerves through' sudden :right. I was then but -yen years of age, and •om that time onwards Ltil lately, when I was ared by Dr. Williams' ink pills for pale people, have suffered from heart Lsease. On all occasions had to keep extremely ruiet, as the least excite- lent put me into a fear- ul state. Two years ago Ly complaint was sup- lemented by three more Llments which followed one upon the other— Annie they. dropsy, pleurisy, and rheu- (Front a recent photograph.) matism. From that time I spent most of my life in bed, and although I was in the hospital for four months it seemed as though I must go on without any hope of relief." Asked to describe further the symptoms of her ail- ments, Miss Guy said: "The rheumatism affected me in my ankles and legs, and to walk was the most acute agony; as the pain also affected my hands it was im- possible for me to do any work. The dropsy affected me very severely in the legs, and if I attempted to get out of bed the awful pain made me scream. The attack of pleurisy left me very weak indeed, end I felt as though all my strength had left me, never to return. I had suffered •in this way for a long time and had become a helpless, miserable girl when my father returned home from sea. He was grieved at my appearance, and after talking the matter over he informed me that a friend had told him of the great benefits his wife had derived from Dr. Williams' pink pills for pale people. Father said he, was going out to get some of the pills for me. He did so, and after I had taken three boxes he said anyone could see that they were doing me a great deal of good. All the neighbours as well began to notice the improve- ment in me, and, personally, I commenced to feel very much stronger, and in better health. Dr. Williams' pink pills have done wonders." "And how is your healtb now, after your Unhappy experience of ten years ?" Oh 1" Miss Guy answered, "-I am now as strong as Call be ; I feel healthy; I am able to get about, and all my troubles, including the heart disease, rheumatism, and the other most painful ailments, have quite dis- appeal:ed." _ _</p>
        <p>'Annie Guy lives at 30 Iris-street, Kirkdale, Liverpool- and that she now looks the picture of healthy woman- hood is the most eloquent testimony to Dr. Williams' pink pills for pale people, yet thousands of other ner- vous, weak, pain-worn women have spoken just as enthu siastically of this famous medicine. All disturbances of the nervous system, including St. Vitus' dance,spinal weakness, paralysis, locomotor ataxy, hysteria, and lack of energy are dispelled by the strength-giving powers of Dr. Williams' pink pills (they are not purgative) ; .and by enriching the blood they have cureil repeatedly anaimia,,pale and sallow complexion, indigestion,eczema, "decline" and incipient consumption. Obtainable direct from Dr. Williams Medicine company, Holborn-viaduct, London, on receipt of two and nine fnr one box, or for six boxes thirteen and nine, but note that substitutes cwhich never cure) are sometimes offered by traders, so readers should always ask for the genuine Dr. Williams' pink pills for pale people, and insist on having them. By doing so they will study their own welfare.</p>
